<title>GREECE: BANK OF GREECE DRAINS 14-DAY FUNDS AT 11.88PCT.</title>
<headline>BANK OF GREECE DRAINS 14-DAY FUNDS AT 11.88PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Greece drained 200 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at a weighted average interest rate of 11.88 percent, it said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Payment date is March 12 and maturity value date March 26.</p>
<p>Accepted bids for the 14-day depo tender ranged from 11.85 to 11.90 percent, the central bank said. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
